Canadian securities and related post-trade processes."},"local_id":"reading_a","questions":["Is client engagement a condition of readiness for every LC or only where clients are potentially affected?","How should cross-currency FX T+2 mismatch controls be evidenced?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT] The selected LC readiness control is compliant when the LC has assessed impact and readiness, can complete post-trade settlement on time, has liquidity/funding and staffing/training controls, and has engaged potentially affected clients.","subject":"Licensed corporation operational readiness"},"protocol":"legalmath.search.v1","role":"adversarial-investigator","source_packet":{"authority":"RETAINED_SOURCE","dependencies":[],"family_ids":["scope","definitions","exceptions","modality","time","dependencies"],"selected_slice":"Selected operational readiness obligations on licensed corporations for the settlement transition, including the Canada footnote and different foreign-exchange cycle. Distinguish optional staffing measures from duties; preserve discretion and definitions.","source_key":"assurance.f0480407f31574a227c8763c","units":[{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=24EC16 chars 0:496","normative":true,"span":{"end":496,"id":"s.d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u0.0","page":1,"quote_sha256":"cf0e409e80633eca9dc26f86359e38ac424fb70f6b0c47c7ba827d7fa3f90700","raw_sha256":"268cbf7137c108f5a0246a76a396c29584c8c7724542138dbc9186e28bd91def","source_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b","start":0,"text_sha256":"27808e1b78f37e5fda442faa6ede66cc88107bdb91a0e8e286aed3d76d8b3156"},"text":"Effective 28 May 2024, the standard settlement cycle for transactions in US securities1 will be shortened from two business days after the trade date (T+2) to one business day after trading (T+1) (the Transition)2. As such, the timeline for completing post-trade settlement processes3 will be compressed. The Securities and Futures Commission (SFC) is of the view that the impact of the Transition may be particularly significant for market participants in Hong Kong due to time zone differences.","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u0.0"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=24EC16 chars 498:877","normative":true,"span":{"end":877,"id":"s.d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498","page":1,"quote_sha256":"4dc81bd9f7e00c84870ac20575b527d3a8083cf075a32fe1051f8292675f9632","raw_sha256":"268cbf7137c108f5a0246a76a396c29584c8c7724542138dbc9186e28bd91def","source_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b","start":498,"text_sha256":"27808e1b78f37e5fda442faa6ede66cc88107bdb91a0e8e286aed3d76d8b3156"},"text":"In this connection, the SFC wishes to remind licensed corporations (LCs) to assess the impact of the Transition on their businesses and take appropriate measures to maintain their smooth and effective operations after the Transition. These include enhancing their operational processes, technological infrastructure and systems as well as staffing arrangements where appropriate.","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=24EC16 chars 879:993","normative":true,"span":{"end":993,"id":"s.d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u2.879","page":1,"quote_sha256":"b9550aab034a1d3e4c35000e73e4c197779762d46892bf0f6652a1a811d53b3e","raw_sha256":"268cbf7137c108f5a0246a76a396c29584c8c7724542138dbc9186e28bd91def","source_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b","start":879,"text_sha256":"27808e1b78f37e5fda442faa6ede66cc88107bdb91a0e8e286aed3d76d8b3156"},"text":"LCs should assess their readiness and ensure they are able to cope with the shortened settlement cycle, including:","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u2.879"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=24EC16 chars 996:1446","normative":true,"span":{"end":1446,"id":"s.d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996","page":1,"quote_sha256":"a9e445b118cdb24f25fe2163b8232c0490234ebd63255a268e9af811d28c2d6d","raw_sha256":"268cbf7137c108f5a0246a76a396c29584c8c7724542138dbc9186e28bd91def","source_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b","start":996,"text_sha256":"27808e1b78f37e5fda442faa6ede66cc88107bdb91a0e8e286aed3d76d8b3156"},"text":"Reviewing their liquidity risk management practices and ensuring the necessary funding is available for settling US securities transactions on time. For cross-currency transactions, given that the standard settlement cycle for foreign-exchange transactions remains at T+2, LCs should be mindful of potential liquidity mismatches and settlement failures arising from the different settlement cycles for US securities and foreign-exchange transactions;","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=24EC16 chars 1448:1914","normative":true,"span":{"end":1914,"id":"s.d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448","page":1,"quote_sha256":"f69c40f41fe2c639638feb25b4674b5d0ab9f9567176506aa2d2e9283a1e2456","raw_sha256":"268cbf7137c108f5a0246a76a396c29584c8c7724542138dbc9186e28bd91def","source_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b","start":1448,"text_sha256":"27808e1b78f37e5fda442faa6ede66cc88107bdb91a0e8e286aed3d76d8b3156"},"text":"Ensuring the availability of staff to complete the post-trade settlement processes within the shortened timeframe. LCs may consider adjusting their staff’s work shifts, extending working hours or arranging evening or morning duties in conjunction with automating their operational processes to enable timely trade settlements. Adequate training should be provided to enable relevant staff to effectively perform their duties under the shortened settlement cycle; and","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=24EC16 chars 1916:2113","normative":true,"span":{"end":2113,"id":"s.d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u5.1916","page":1,"quote_sha256":"faf639f4cadfe3c8bef2df29f7b5033e716bc90d395f1a2b6dd9b42b0683cda9","raw_sha256":"268cbf7137c108f5a0246a76a396c29584c8c7724542138dbc9186e28bd91def","source_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b","start":1916,"text_sha256":"27808e1b78f37e5fda442faa6ede66cc88107bdb91a0e8e286aed3d76d8b3156"},"text":"Proactively engaging and communicating with their clients who are potentially affected by the Transition in order to raise their awareness and facilitate their preparations for a smooth transition.","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u5.1916"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=24EC16 chars 2116:2264","normative":true,"span":{"end":2264,"id":"s.d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u6.2116","page":1,"quote_sha256":"eda5dd84c8a68a63054d3803736a20de6023247e4040bea2c73fa8393fb43016","raw_sha256":"268cbf7137c108f5a0246a76a396c29584c8c7724542138dbc9186e28bd91def","source_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b","start":2116,"text_sha256":"27808e1b78f37e5fda442faa6ede66cc88107bdb91a0e8e286aed3d76d8b3156"},"text":"In addition, management companies of SFC-authorised funds (Funds), particularly those with considerable exposures to US securities, are reminded to:","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u6.2116"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=24EC16 chars 2267:2497","normative":true,"span":{"end":2497,"id":"s.d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u7.2267","page":1,"quote_sha256":"536f75ca0df2d162a620a817e6ae16300855a265d81a971ee63603d6e2814880","raw_sha256":"268cbf7137c108f5a0246a76a396c29584c8c7724542138dbc9186e28bd91def","source_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b","start":2267,"text_sha256":"27808e1b78f37e5fda442faa6ede66cc88107bdb91a0e8e286aed3d76d8b3156"},"text":"Carefully assess the impact of the Transition on their Funds, including any potential mismatches in settlement cycles relating to the deployment of subscription money or sale proceeds from non-US markets to purchase US securities;","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u7.2267"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=24EC16 chars 2499:2769","normative":true,"span":{"end":2769,"id":"s.d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u8.2499","page":1,"quote_sha256":"28043296ce8f15f49a0a22887f84ad3bb425e65bae447cf48b63fb9d21d6e010","raw_sha256":"268cbf7137c108f5a0246a76a396c29584c8c7724542138dbc9186e28bd91def","source_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b","start":2499,"text_sha256":"27808e1b78f37e5fda442faa6ede66cc88107bdb91a0e8e286aed3d76d8b3156"},"text":"Make appropriate arrangements where necessary, such as expanding pre-funding facilities and allocating additional staff to handle the compressed settlement timeline, to ensure that the Funds’ operations remain fair and orderly, and in the best interest of investors; and","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u8.2499"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=24EC16 chars 2771:2993","normative":true,"span":{"end":2993,"id":"s.d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u9.2771","page":1,"quote_sha256":"a5b8b48dace5dfffbd797ba775346a80e6a5bf9384245556370f9062d1b4cbc7","raw_sha256":"268cbf7137c108f5a0246a76a396c29584c8c7724542138dbc9186e28bd91def","source_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b","start":2771,"text_sha256":"27808e1b78f37e5fda442faa6ede66cc88107bdb91a0e8e286aed3d76d8b3156"},"text":"Give early alerts to the SFC and investors about any intended changes, issues or untoward circumstances arising from the Transition that may materially affect the Funds and investors, and take remedial actions accordingly.","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u9.2771"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=24EC16 chars 2996:3079","normative":true,"span":{"end":3079,"id":"s.d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u10.2996","page":1,"quote_sha256":"3f15ef85a8de1db6a7438a8ff06266e489facdd9f2627f501716eefb36bda6de","raw_sha256":"268cbf7137c108f5a0246a76a396c29584c8c7724542138dbc9186e28bd91def","source_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b","start":2996,"text_sha256":"27808e1b78f37e5fda442faa6ede66cc88107bdb91a0e8e286aed3d76d8b3156"},"text":"The SFC will continue to monitor market developments in relation to the Transition.","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u10.2996"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=24EC16 chars 3083:3171","normative":true,"span":{"end":3171,"id":"s.d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u11.3083","page":1,"quote_sha256":"0e3225addfcc2663ed547268443c0eda4c4b22cc50e1f858008119256b3a532c","raw_sha256":"268cbf7137c108f5a0246a76a396c29584c8c7724542138dbc9186e28bd91def","source_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b","start":3083,"text_sha256":"27808e1b78f37e5fda442faa6ede66cc88107bdb91a0e8e286aed3d76d8b3156"},"text":"Intermediaries Supervision Department                       Investment Products Division","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u11.3083"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=24EC16 chars 3172:3289","normative":true,"span":{"end":3289,"id":"s.d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u12.3172","page":1,"quote_sha256":"785d44c652b65df6766b7210a6c4ad86fba361d3eb7c7e10d9dae247a1b416f1","raw_sha256":"268cbf7137c108f5a0246a76a396c29584c8c7724542138dbc9186e28bd91def","source_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b","start":3172,"text_sha256":"27808e1b78f37e5fda442faa6ede66cc88107bdb91a0e8e286aed3d76d8b3156"},"text":"Intermediaries Division                                                             Securities and Futures Commission","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u12.3172"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=24EC16 chars 3290:3323","normative":true,"span":{"end":3323,"id":"s.d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u13.3290","page":1,"quote_sha256":"88e2bc94e9edc39f2ac1cdaaea86b44ab5ea59b31c446f69591f21bf460b005e","raw_sha256":"268cbf7137c108f5a0246a76a396c29584c8c7724542138dbc9186e28bd91def","source_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b","start":3290,"text_sha256":"27808e1b78f37e5fda442faa6ede66cc88107bdb91a0e8e286aed3d76d8b3156"},"text":"Securities and Futures Commission","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u13.3290"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=24EC16 chars 3336:3397","normative":true,"span":{"end":3397,"id":"s.d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u14.3336","page":1,"quote_sha256":"970b888c7fb9ee70753be5ec1f4519ef5882482f0389de2c2b6bd2953209f124","raw_sha256":"268cbf7137c108f5a0246a76a396c29584c8c7724542138dbc9186e28bd91def","source_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b","start":3336,"text_sha256":"27808e1b78f37e5fda442faa6ede66cc88107bdb91a0e8e286aed3d76d8b3156"},"text":"1 Such as equities, bonds, exchange-traded funds and options.","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u14.3336"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=24EC16 chars 3399:3565","normative":true,"span":{"end":3565,"id":"s.d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399","page":1,"quote_sha256":"41ae1c2b09e63f2b585c27f44fc9995a349b47efba29c2fb6ae9b1cd22c8649b","raw_sha256":"268cbf7137c108f5a0246a76a396c29584c8c7724542138dbc9186e28bd91def","source_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b","start":3399,"text_sha256":"27808e1b78f37e5fda442faa6ede66cc88107bdb91a0e8e286aed3d76d8b3156"},"text":"2 The settlement cycle in Canada will transition to T+1 on 27 May 2024. The reference to the Transition in this circular includes the transition in the US and Canada.","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399"},{"locator":"https://apps.sfc.hk/edistributionWeb/gateway/EN/circular/doc?refNo=24EC16 chars 3567:3626","normative":true,"span":{"end":3626,"id":"s.d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u16.3567","page":1,"quote_sha256":"b95ba5154d61b6ce5b3c42cb2e0d34302fce03407cd3d7fe99d810d188e7efab","raw_sha256":"268cbf7137c108f5a0246a76a396c29584c8c7724542138dbc9186e28bd91def","source_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b","start":3567,"text_sha256":"27808e1b78f37e5fda442faa6ede66cc88107bdb91a0e8e286aed3d76d8b3156"},"text":"3 Including trade allocation, confirmation and affirmation.","unit_id":"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u16.3567"}]},"task":"REFINE"},"run_id":"run.ed16031b15a945ad9771bf61094e0c1e","schema":{"$defs":{"DimensionFinding":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"dimension":{"enum":["scope","definitions","exceptions","modality","time","dependencies"],"title":"Dimension","type":"string"},"explanation":{"maxLength":20000,"minLength":1,"title":"Explanation","type":"string"},"source_unit_ids":{"items":{"pattern":"^[a-z][a-z0-9_.:-]{0,127}$","type":"string"},"maxItems":100,"minItems":1,"title":"Source Unit Ids","type":"array"},"status":{"enum":["PROPOSED","AMBIGUOUS","NOT_APPLICABLE"],"title":"Status","type":"string"}},"required":["dimension","sta